<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Fire TV (Amazon Appstore) flavor overlay.

    The main manifest requests the TV-provider EPG permissions
    (WRITE_EPG_DATA / READ_EPG_DATA) so the Google TV "Watch Next" /
    Continue-Watching row works. But the Amazon Appstore treats an app
    requesting WRITE_EPG_DATA as requiring "a Fire TV device that supports
    EPG integration" and filters the app off the large majority of Fire TV
    hardware (Sticks, most Cubes, most TVs). OnScreen is a VOD library, not
    a live-channel/TIF app, so those permissions buy nothing on Fire OS.

    Strip them from the firetv flavor to restore full Fire TV device
    coverage. The googletv flavor keeps them, so Watch Next is unaffected on
    Google TV / Android TV. See clients/firetv/README.md and
    app/build.gradle.kts (productFlavors) for the build wiring.
-->
<!--
    tools:ignore — two false positives, both verified against the merge output,
    both the same root cause.

    Lint evaluates a flavor overlay in ISOLATION. This file contains only two
    permission removals: no activity, so MissingLeanbackLauncher concludes the
    app has no LEANBACK_LAUNCHER entry point; and no uses-feature, so
    ImpliedTouchscreenHardware concludes touchscreen was never marked optional.
    Both anchor their report to <manifest> here. The firetvRelease MERGED
    manifest has all three elements and is correct:

        uses-feature android.software.leanback  required=false
        uses-feature android.hardware.touchscreen required=false
        activity tv.onscreen.android.ui.MainActivity
          categories: LEANBACK_LAUNCHER, DEFAULT, BROWSABLE

    This predates the leanback work — the same merge shape (and the same lint
    failure) existed when src/main declared leanback required="false". It went
    unnoticed because the Android TV CI job runs only
    :app:testGoogletvDebugUnitTest, never lint. Suppressed at this element
    rather than in lint.xml so a genuine instance of either check anywhere else
    still fails the build.
-->
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools"
    tools:ignore="MissingLeanbackLauncher,ImpliedTouchscreenHardware">

    <uses-permission
        android:name="com.android.providers.tv.permission.WRITE_EPG_DATA"
        tools:node="remove" />
    <uses-permission
        android:name="com.android.providers.tv.permission.READ_EPG_DATA"
        tools:node="remove" />

</manifest>
